From 7a8e34623fb21aeabf485973dd304d52a06b400f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StefanVonRanda <16295563+StefanVonRanda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add image-to-image and inpainting (--init, --strength,
 --mask) with an MLX VAE encoder

The port had only the FLUX.2 VAE decoder, so nothing could start from an
existing image. vae.py gains the encoder (Downsample/_Down/Encoder, quant_conv)
loaded from the official diffusers VAE file on first use, plus
encode_packed = inverse of decode_packed (posterior mean, 2x2 packing,
batch-norm normalisation). pipeline.py: Request.init_image/strength/mask,
_sample starts at sigma index round((1-strength)*steps) from
(1-sigma)*init + sigma*noise and, with a mask, re-blends the unmasked region
onto the init trajectory after every Euler step; decoded pixels outside the
mask are copied from the init. CLI: --init PATH, --strength F, --mask PATH;
the sidecar records init/strength/mask.

Checked: encode->decode of a 512x512 render gives 40.8 dB PSNR (torch
reference: 40.9 dB); packed+normalised latents match diffusers
AutoencoderKLFlux2 fp32 to max abs diff 0.024, mean 0.0019; img2img at
strength 0.5 keeps the composition (5.4 s, 7.9 GB peak, compact tier, 8-step
DMD); inpainting with a rectangle mask rewrote the sign text and left every
pixel outside the mask identical (numpy check). pytest tests/: 24 passed.
Not checked: images larger than 1024^2 through the strip-wise encoder, and
img2img parity against a PyTorch run of the full pipeline.
